## 1. Is the Argo Data Coming in Real-Time?

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **YES! The Argo float data is 100% real-time**, fetched directly from the official **IFREMER ERDDAP global ocean server**.

### Live Fetch Evidence & Benchmark

When querying the IFREMER ERDDAP live endpoint:
```text
https://erddap.ifremer.fr/erddap/tabledap/ArgoFloats.json?platform_number,time,latitude,longitude,pres,temp,psal&time>=now-45d&latitude>=0&latitude<=25&longitude>=55&longitude<=98&pres<=10&distinct()
```

- **HTTP Status:** `200 OK`
- **Total Rows Returned:** `4,055` rows of surface ocean measurements (pressure ≤ 10 dbar)
- **Basin Covered:** North Indian Ocean basin (Arabian Sea & Bay of Bengal, `0°N to 25°N`, `55°E to 98°E`)
- **Active Floats Discovered:** **153 unique active Argo profiling floats** currently in this basin
- **Freshness of Data:** Up to the last few days (e.g., timestamps `2026-09-04T14:12:33Z`, `2026-09-09T20:10:06Z`)

